+The default environment is configured in [launchSettings.json](src/DocumentManagementSystem.Api/Properties/launchSettings.json). The application enables Swagger only when `ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT` is `Development`.
+## JWT authentication
+
+The Sprint 2 API uses database-backed users and JWT Bearer authentication.
+
+1. Start the complete application with `docker compose up -d --build`.
+2. Open `http://localhost/register` and create an account.
+3. The registration response signs the user in immediately and stores the JWT in the frontend session.
+4. Existing users can sign in at `http://localhost/login`.
+5. Documents and collections require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; `/health`, `/auth/register` and `/auth/login` remain public.
+
+Passwords are never stored as plain text. ASP.NET Core `PasswordHasher<User>` hashes passwords before the user is persisted in PostgreSQL. Usernames are unique case-insensitively.
+
+For Docker, override the signing key in real environments:
+
+```powershell
+$env:JWT_KEY="replace-this-with-a-long-random-secret-at-least-32-bytes"
+docker compose up -d --build
+```
+
+Run the end-to-end authentication smoke test from Git Bash/WSL with `./scripts/smoke-test.sh`.
